[engl]
{100}{}{Over}
{200}{}{You see the Overseer.}
{1000}{}{[AUTO-GENERATED SKELETON: replace this entry with the NPC's initial greeting and
conditions.]}
{1010}{}{Last words of the overseer.}
{1020}{}{Betrayed the vault 13}
{1030}{}{rebellion quest}
{1040}{}{Waterchip found}
{1050}{}{Waterchip still not be found}
{1060}{}{Waterchip still not be found 2}
{1070}{}{Waterchip still not be found 3}
{1080}{}{Water caravan 1}
{1090}{}{Water caravan 2}
{1100}{}{Mutants not finished}
{1110}{}{Mutants lab quest start.}
{1120}{}{Mutant laboratory in course.}
{1130}{}{Mutant lab quest in course.}
{1140}{}{Mutant leader quest in course.}
{2000}{}{You've done it! That's . . . wonderful. Amazing! I'm so proud of what you've accomplished, what you've endured.}
{2010}{}{...}
{3000}{}{There's no way the people of the Vault can ever thank you enough for what you've done. You've saved all our lives. Who knows, maybe even saved the human race. [The Overseer sighs.] That makes the rest of this even harder.}
{3010}{}{...}
{4000}{}{Everyone will want to talk to you. Every youngster will look up to you, and want to
emulate you. And then what?}
{4010}{}{...}
{5000}{}{They'll want to leave. What happens to the Vault if we lose the best of a generation?
What if we are the only safe place in the world? You just gave us back all these lives .
. . I can't take the chance of losing them.}
{5010}{}{...}
{6000}{}{I've made a lot of tough decisions since I took this position. But none of them harder than this one. You saved us, but you'll kill us. I'm sorry. You're a hero . . . and you have to leave.}
{6010}{}{[Done.]}
{7000}{}{What's wrong with you?! You turned against us?! I can not allow that.}
{7010}{}{Yeah, well I guess you'll have to find someone else to do your dirty work.}
{8000}{}{We can't have this. Not now. Not with everything else going on. The rules of the Vault are there for our protection and the survival of our species.}
{8010}{}{[Done.]}
{9000}{}{Have you found the chip?}
{9010}{}{Yes.}
{9020}{}{Yes, but I think we should talk more about letting people leave the Vault.}
{9030}{}{Nuh-huh!}
{10000}{}{Okey-dokey. One moment, the chip is initializing. Here - here - here - There it goes . .
. Self-test is green . . . re-boot is good . . . Hah! It's working! And it looks like we
have a winner! Haha! [The overseer sighs with relief.] You -- you've saved us. You've
done it!}
{10010}{}{Ahh, it was nothing.}
{10020}{}{You're welcome.}
{11000}{}{Nothing? No, oh no! It was something. Don't downplay what you've done. You've saved a lot of lives. All right, now we need a report on what's out there. Please go to the library.}
{11010}{}{Ok.}
{12000}{}{You saved the Vault. You should be proud. But now, we need your report. We'll get it from you in the library. Please go there now.}
{12010}{}{Ok.}
{13000}{}{Well, you've certainly earned that right. But let's take care of survival first. Give me
the chip and we'll discuss this when you give your report.}
{13010}{}{Fair enough.}
{13020}{}{I don't know.}
{14000}{}{Please, the chip!}
{14010}{}{Fair enough.}
{14020}{}{I don't know.}
{15000}{}{Oh, that's great! Can I have the chip, please?}
{15010}{}{Nungh.}
{16000}{}{No, not that. I want the com-pu-ter chip.}
{16010}{}{Nungh.}
{17000}{}{No. The chip.}
{17010}{}{Nungh.}
{18000}{}{Just-give-me-the-chip!}
{18010}{}{Nungh.}
{19000}{}{Thank you. Now, go to the library and rest for a while, ok?}
{19010}{}{Nuh-huh, uh-nuh?}
{19020}{}{Uh, nuh? Nuh-uh-uh-nuh.}
{20000}{}{Yes, you can touch things.}
{20010}{}{[Done.]}
{21000}{}{Oh, yes. You did good and I'm sure you have a lot to tell.}
{21010}{}{[Done.]}
{22000}{}{You're back! And in one piece! How goes the search?}
{22010}{}{Not good, but I noticed the radiation count is low. Why don't we just move the people
out of the vault?}
{22020}{}{I haven't found the chip yet. Can't we just make a replacement?}
{22030}{}{Nothing yet.}
{22040}{}{Nuh.}
{23000}{}{We've debated this before. You ought to know now, after being out there! You think the
rest of us could survive that? Besides, I'd be out of a job! I'm management! It's not
like I know how to do anything useful!}
{23010}{}{We agree on that.}
{24000}{}{Look, I know it's got to be tough. But we're counting on you. And we're running out of
time. Please! Keep trying!}
{24010}{}{I understand. I'll work harder to find the chip.}
{25000}{}{Ahh, you never did listen to me. We don't have the necessary parts anymore. We've used
up all the supplies required.}
{25010}{}{Oh, ok. Thanks.}
{26000}{}{Well, do you have the chip?}
{26010}{}{Not yet. Sorry.}
{26020}{}{I still say we just pack everybody up and move out of here.}
{26030}{}{No, but I have a lot of other things to tell you!}
{26040}{}{Nuh.}
{27000}{}{[The Overseer sighs.] Don't be sorry. I know you're trying your best and that means a
lot. But you can't give up now.}
{27010}{}{[Done.]}
{28000}{}{This isn't the best time to debate that. Get the chip, give us the option. Most of these
people, including me, won't survive out there.}
{28010}{}{OK, I'll go see if I can find it.}
{29000}{}{We have no time, no options. I know it's a lot of responsibility for you, but we have no
choice. We need the chip now.}
{29010}{}{[Done.]}
{30000}{}{Please tell me you've found the chip.}
{30010}{}{No, but I've seen some amazing things!}
{30020}{}{Sorry, haven't been able to track it down yet.}
{30030}{}{Nope.}
{30040}{}{Nuh-uh.}
{31000}{}{We don't have time for this! We need the chip. Time's running out. [Sigh]}
{31010}{}{[Done.]}
{32000}{}{Is there some problem, do you need more equipment? Is there anything we can do to help?}
{32010}{}{Nope, just going to take some time. It's a big world out there.}
{32020}{}{I could use some more stuff.}
{32030}{}{Yeah, you could get off your fannies and help.}
{33000}{}{Do your best. Remember, we're all counting on you.}
{33010}{}{[Done.]}
{34000}{}{Here, take the last of our ammo and portable healing supplies. We're in trouble. Hurry!}
{34010}{}{[Done.]}
{35000}{}{Do what? With who? Anyone else would be less qualified and have less supplies. It'd be suicide.}
{35010}{}{Your choice. I'll do my best, but I don't know if it'll be enough.}
{35020}{}{I understand.}
{36000}{}{It has to be. If you fail, so does the Vault.}
{36010}{}{Got it.}
{36020}{}{Whatever.}
{37000}{}{Good, then get going!}
{37010}{}{[Done.]}
{38000}{}{Well, keep looking. Time's growing short.}
{38010}{}{[Done.]}
{39000}{}{The water caravans from this Hub place have started to arrive. I've been running the
figures and I've got some disturbing news.}
{39010}{}{What's that?}
{39020}{}{Huh?}
{40000}{}{The caravan water will maintain our current supply, but not increase it substantially.
And these Hub merchants are charging us an arm and leg. This helps and we're thankful
for that, but it's not a solution.}
{40010}{}{Ok.}
{40020}{}{There's something else, isn't there?}
{41000}{}{Keep looking for a replacement chip. It's the only way we can maintain our independence
and the security that comes with our seclusion.}
{41010}{}{[Done.]}
{42000}{}{We're taking a terrible risk by showing these people the way to our vault. I understand your choice, and it may be what saves us. But I'm worried. Can we trust these people?}
{42010}{}{I trust them.}
{42020}{}{I understand.}
{43000}{}{I'm sure you do, but we need that replacement chip for our long-term survival and
economic stability. We don't produce as many goods as we need to pay for this water, and
soon we won't be able to pay. Find the chip.}
{43010}{}{[Done.]}
{44000}{}{I'm sure you do. You must also understand our need for that replacement chip. Please
keep looking.}
{44010}{}{[Done.]}
{45000}{}{Oh, never mind. Just try and find the water chip. Get the chip. We still need it.}
{45010}{}{[Done.]}
{46000}{}{Please keep looking for the water chip. These water caravans are going to cause us problems in the long run.}
{46010}{}{[Done.]}
{47000}{}{What news do you have of the mutants?}
{47010}{}{I wasted the head SOB.}
{47020}{}{I've killed the Master, the mutant leader.}
{47030}{}{Nuh, ungh. Uh-nuh, nuh.}
{48000}{}{Excellent! What about the laboratory? Did you destroy that, too?}
{48010}{}{No.}
{49000}{}{Go back out and find it. It needs to be destroyed for the vault to be safe. Try to the
west, most of the mutants seem to be there.}
{49010}{}{[Done.]}
{50000}{}{What's that? You've killed the mutant leader?}
{50010}{}{Uh-huh, nuh, huh. Nuh-nuh.}
{51000}{}{There are still more mutants appearing? You need to destroy their vats? Great job! Go
back out there and take care of it.}
{51010}{}{[Done.]}
{52000}{}{I uh, I just wanted to let you know that the water supply has stabilized. Actually, we're rebuilding our reserves. You did great . . . I uh, I am a little concerned, however.}
{52010}{}{About what?}
{52020}{}{Huh?}
{53000}{}{I' I don't like your reports. What was in the reports, that is. Heh. In fact, they
scared the heck out of me. It's those mutants. I've done some calculations and, well,
I've come to an unpleasant conclusion.}
{53010}{}{What's that?}
{54000}{}{[Sigh] The mutant population is far greater than could be expected by natural growth or mutations. This leads me to believe in -- I don't really understand it. But it looks like someone's generating new mutants. And at a startling rate.}
{54010}{}{Say again? Without the confusion?}
{54020}{}{Must be a lab somewhere then.}
{55000}{}{Someone's making mutants!}
{55010}{}{What do I need to do?}
{56000}{}{As long as someone is creating hostile mutants at this rate, the Vault's safety is at
stake! Find and destroy this lab as soon as you can.}
{56010}{}{Ok.}
{56020}{}{Once more into the breach, my friend.}
{57000}{}{You have no idea how sorry I am to send you back out.}
{57010}{}{[Done.]}
{58000}{}{Exactly! And as you've probably guessed, none of these mutations could have occurred
naturally, even with the radiation from the war.}
{58010}{}{What do you want me to do about it?}
{59000}{}{Oh, yeah. Hmm . . . I' I' I' It's like this. There is a bad place where the bad mutants
come from. It is bad. Vault is good. Please, go destroy bad place.}
{59010}{}{[Done.]}
{60000}{}{Has the mutant laboratory been discovered yet? Even better, tell me it's been destroyed.}
{60010}{}{No.}
{60020}{}{Nungh.}
{60030}{}{Not yet, but I've got some good leads.}
{60040}{}{Nope, I'm a little lost.}
{61000}{}{Well, keep searching.}
{61010}{}{[Done.]}
{62000}{}{Good. But hurry, the more time they have to produce them, the harder they'll be to stop.}
{62010}{}{[Done.]}
{63000}{}{Well, based on the information you provided about population density, I think you should
concentrate your search to the west.}
{63010}{}{[Done.]}
{64000}{}{What news of the mutants?}
{64010}{}{I blew them up.}
{64020}{}{Nuhh!}
{64030}{}{The mutant vats have been destroyed.}
{65000}{}{All of them?}
{65010}{}{Well, all of them at the vats.}
{65020}{}{Uh, nuh-nuh.}
{66000}{}{What about the mutant leader? What about this so-called Master?}
{66010}{}{Far as I know, he's still alive.}
{66020}{}{Uh-nuh-nuh.}
{67000}{}{He must be stopped. If not, he could rebuild his empire of mutants and would certainly
strike back at us. The vault will not be safe until the Master is dead.}
{67010}{}{[Done.]}
{68000}{}{Is the mutant leader . . . taken care of?}
{68010}{}{No.}
{68020}{}{Nuh.}
{68030}{}{He will be . . . soon.}
{69000}{}{I know this has been hard on you. But this Master's the type who'll rebuild his mutant
army. Then he'll come for us. Please, go out and finish the job.}
{69010}{}{[Done.]}
{70000}{}{Well, Th' Tha' That's great. That's very good. You sound like you're in control out there. Please, finish this up soon so that you and I can . . . When you're out there, remember, the people of the Vault know you've saved them.}
{70010}{}{[Done.]}

